MST we need all pairs? Actually HDBSCAN mutual reachability uses all pairwise distances. If some distances are missing, we cannot compute all edges. So we must assume that distances list contains all pairs (complete graph). The fixtures show 10 distances for 5 nodes, which is all pairs (10). So we can assume that. We'll compute for each pair in distances list, but also need to ensure we handle self? Not needed.\n\nFor canonicalization: Edge (u,v) with u and v strings. We'll ensure u < v lexicographically (string compare). Then mutual reachability = max(core_u, core_v, dist). Store (u, v, weight). Then sort edges list by (weight, u, v). Then run Kruskal.\n\nUse union-find with path compression and union by rank.\n\nReturn mst_edges as list of [u, v, weight] and total_weight (sum of weights).\n\nIf after processing all edges, number of edges in MST != len(nodes)-1, then graph is disconnected -> raise ValueError.\n\nWe must use only standard library. Use math? Not needed. Use json for output? The function should return dictionary directly, that will be serialized by evaluator.\n\nEdge cases: nodes list may be empty? Not likely. But handle: if nodes length <=1, MST has 0 edges, total_weight 0. But then distances list might be empty. Need to handle. The schema expects mst_edges as array (could be empty). We'll handle.\n\nAlso core_distance dictionary may have all nodes.\n\nImplementation details:\n\n- Parse case: case is dict with keys: nodes (list), core_distance (dict), distances (list of lists). \n- Build lookup for core distances: core = case['core_distance'].\n- edges = []\n- For each [u, v, d] in distances:\n   if u == v: skip? Not present.\n   if u > v: swap.\n   w = max(core[u], core[v], d)\n   edges.append((u, v, w))\n- Sort edges by (w, u, v)\n- Initialize DSU for node labels (set of all nodes from case['nodes']). Use dict mapping node to parent and rank.\n- selected = []\n- total = 0.0\n- For (u,v,w) in edges:\n   if find(u) != find(v):\n        union(u,v)\n  